; secrets.ini.example — template. Copy it to `secrets.ini` and fill in the values.
;
;     cp secrets.ini.example secrets.ini
;
; `secrets.ini` is in .gitignore and is NOT versioned. This file (the
; .example) IS versioned, so never put real credentials here.
;
; PlatformIO loads it via `extra_configs` in platformio.ini, and both the
; firmware's `-D` flags and the OTA upload's `--auth` come from it. If the
; file or a key is missing, the build fails loudly (see the #error in
; src/config.h) instead of flashing a node that can't connect.
;
; ─── Watch out for two characters ─────────────────────────────────────────────
;
;   $   PlatformIO uses it to interpolate (${...}). If a password has one,
;       escape it as $$ .
;   "   breaks the -D. Avoid double quotes in passwords.
;
; Spaces do work (the SSID below has three) because platformio.ini wraps
; each flag in single quotes.
;
; ─── What this does NOT solve ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; It gets credentials out of the repo, which is the real problem when the
; code lives on GitHub. It does NOT get them out of the binary: the compiled
; firmware carries them in plain text, and anyone with physical access to
; the node can dump the flash. That would require NVS provisioning or ESP32
; flash encryption.

[secrets]
wifi_ssid     = MyWiFiNetwork
wifi_password = changeme
mqtt_user     = weather_station_iot
mqtt_password = changeme
ota_password  = changeme
